    83	## Parallel day (D172–D183)
    84	
    85	The replay runs the parallel day by default (D183: Alex chose it to converge faster); `scripts/replay.py --workers 1` runs the serial path, needed to resume a day a serial run left unfinished. Measured live on the complete July 27 day (53 items), three serial against three parallel trials interleaved ([result](../poc/reports/2026-10-26-e2e-parallel/results.md)): median 501.8 s → 112.5 s, **4.46× end to end**, 5.91× for item work; daily judging (~37–40 s) is the same code in both modes. Every trial's audit is clean; each parallel trial's runner accepted exactly the rebuilt exact-prefix request for all 53 items; each trial's answers replayed through the other mode give an identical ledger. Drift from the recorded sequential golden is inside the serial trials' own spread. The product entry point (`--workers 16`) ran the same day live in 135.5 s with the same checks clean. On recorded answers the parallel day equals the golden in all ten tables (D180, and again on the promoted module).
